---
import Arrow from "../components/arrow.astro";
import AsciiSculpture from "../components/ascii-sculpture";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/site-layout.astro";
import { site } from "../site";

const libraries = [
  { description: "Bring AI into the work.", name: "Agents", path: "agents" },
  {
    description: "Give a process staying power.",
    name: "Workflows",
    path: "workflows",
  },
  {
    description: "Choose the right intelligence.",
    name: "Models",
    path: "models",
  },
  {
    description: "Keep your work grounded.",
    name: "Workspaces",
    path: "workspaces",
  },
  {
    description: "Keep what you create.",
    name: "Artifacts",
    path: "artifacts",
  },
  { description: "Give ideas room to run.", name: "Sandbox", path: "sandbox" },
];
---

<SiteLayout>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Craft the<br />way you<br /><span class="work-word">work.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-description">Open-source local tools.<br />Built to run on your machine.</p>
      <a class="button" href="#tools">Explore the tools <Arrow /></a>
      <p class="hero-footnote">Yours to use, inspect, and make your own.</p>
    </div>
    <AsciiSculpture client:visible />
    <div class="hero-caption">
      <p>Workflows, codebase maps &amp; building blocks.<br />On your machine. In your hands.</p>
      <a href="#tools" aria-label="Scroll to the tools"><span>See what’s on the workbench</span><Arrow /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section" id="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="tools-title">A few good tools.<br />A lot of possibilities.</h2>
        <p>Start with what’s here. Make it part of your practice.<br />Our first tools are for working with code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-shelf">
        <article class="tool tool-marbles">
          <div class="tool-art workflow-art" aria-label="Illustration of a repeatable workflow: gather, shape, make">
            <div class="workflow-path" aria-hidden="true"><span>gather</span><i></i><span>shape</span><i></i><span>make</span></div>
            <pre aria-hidden="true" class="marble-specimen">{`           . . : : : . .
       . : + # # # # # + : .
     . + # @ @ @ @ @ @ # # + .
    : # @ @ @ @ @ @ @ # # # # :
   + @ @ @ @ @ @ @ # # # # + + +
   # @ @ @ @ @ # # # # # + + : :
   # @ @ @ # # # # # + + : : . .
    + # # # # # + + : : : . .
     : + # + + : : : . . .
       . : : : : . . .
           . . . .`}</pre>
            <span class="specimen-caption">Small steps. Something bigger.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-copy">
            <div class="tool-title"><h3>Marbles</h3><span>Repeatable work</span></div>
            <p>Give the work you do again and again a shape. Compose steps, workflows, and agents in TypeScript, then run them on your machine.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href={`${site.docs}marbles/`}>Make a workflow <Arrow /></a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="tool tool-atlas">
          <div class="tool-art atlas-art" aria-label="Illustration of a codebase map with connected packages, files, and dependencies">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 560 310" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".42"><path d="m98 184 129-107 118 121 124-97M98 184l136 64 111-50M227 77l242 24M234 248l235-147" stroke-dasharray="3 5" /></g>
              <g fill="currentColor"><circle cx="98" cy="184" r="8"/><circle cx="227" cy="77" r="12"/><circle cx="345" cy="198" r="17"/><circle cx="469" cy="101" r="7"/><circle cx="234" cy="248" r="6"/></g>
              <g stroke="currentColor"><circle cx="98" cy="184" r="22"/><circle cx="227" cy="77" r="29"/><circle cx="345" cy="198" r="40"/><circle cx="469" cy="101" r="19"/><circle cx="234" cy="248" r="17"/></g>
              <g fill="currentColor" opacity=".5"><circle cx="71" cy="163" r="3"/><circle cx="113" cy="218" r="3"/><circle cx="198" cy="52" r="3"/><circle cx="254" cy="40" r="3"/><circle cx="261" cy="103" r="3"/><circle cx="308" cy="158" r="3"/><circle cx="396" cy="184" r="3"/><circle cx="375" cy="241" r="3"/><circle cx="323" cy="253" r="3"/><circle cx="494" cy="78" r="3"/></g>
            </svg>
            <span class="map-label map-label-packages">packages</span><span class="map-label map-label-files">files</span><span class="specimen-caption">Find your bearings.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-copy">
            <div class="tool-title"><h3>Atlas</h3><span>A wider view</span></div>
            <p>Get to know the code you’re working with. Explore your TypeScript workspace as a map of packages, files, and the connections between them.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href={`${site.docs}atlas/`}>Explore your codebase <Arrow /></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="library-heading"><h3>And the parts to build your own.</h3><p>The shared libraries beneath the tools. Ready to explore in the source.</p></div>
      <div class="library-list">
        {libraries.map((library) => <a href={`${site.repository}/tree/main/packages/${library.path}`}><div><h4>{library.name}</h4><p>{library.description}</p></div><Arrow /></a>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="vision-section wrap" id="vision" aria-labelledby="vision-title">
    <div class="vision-heading"><h2 id="vision-title">The way we make<br />things is a thing<br />we can make.</h2><span class="maker-stamp" aria-hidden="true">Always<br />in the making.</span></div>
    <div class="vision-copy">
      <p class="lead">We’re crafting the tools for crafting.</p>
      <p>Every practice has its tools. The ones you reach for, adapt, and eventually make your own. We think software should work that way, too.</p>
      <p>Foundry is a collection of open-source local tools for shaping how you work. Run them on your machine, work with your own files, and adapt the source to fit your practice. We’re starting with code.</p>
      <p>Use a tool. Take it apart. Build something we haven’t thought of. That’s the idea.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={site.repository}>Take a look inside <Arrow /></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="closing-section" aria-labelledby="closing-title"><div class="wrap closing-content"><h2 id="closing-title">Make something<br />your way.</h2><div><p>A good place to start is a tool you can make your own.</p><a class="button" href={site.docs}>Find your starting point <Arrow /></a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
